# Ed-Fi API v8 pilot kit: smoke-test requests (Task 14, FR-TEST-1..3, 6..8). These are the same
# interactions `smoke-test.sh`/`.ps1` run non-interactively; this file is for a person to run one
# request at a time in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and read the actual responses.
#
# Fill in @key and @secret below before running anything past the token request. Two ways:
#
#   1. File variables (quickest): open .runtime/bootstrap-credentials.json (written by `start` or
#      `bootstrap` -- see bootstrap/README.md) and paste its "key" and "secret" fields into the two
#      lines below.
#   2. A REST Client environment (keeps secrets out of this file): add an environment in
#      .vscode/settings.json's "rest-client.environmentVariables", for example
#        { "$shared": { "key": "...", "secret": "..." } }
#      then pick it from the REST Client status bar and leave @key/@secret blank -- {{key}}/{{secret}}
#      resolve the same way either way. See
#      https://github.com/Huachao/vscode-restclient/blob/master/README.md#environment-variables
#
# Every request below authenticates with the bootstrap (ADMIN) credential -- the only one that
# already exists right after startup (FR-TEST-2). It is broad-access and not representative of a
# participant integration credential (FR-BOOT-7/8); use `new-credential` (Task 13) to provision a
# scoped credential for authorization testing.
#
# @baseUrl is the DMS route through NGINX (PUBLIC_ORIGIN + DMS_PATH_BASE in .env; adjust both if you
# changed either from their defaults). The baseline education organization ids below are the single
# source of truth in bootstrap/baseline-edorgs.json (FR-EDORG-14) -- see http/edorgs.http.

@baseUrl = https://localhost/api
@key =
@secret =

@seaId = 99
@leaId = 9900
@elementarySchoolId = 990001
@middleSchoolId = 990002
@highSchoolId = 990003

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Token (DMS proxies to CMS's /connect/token; spike-notes.md Q7). HTTP Basic auth: REST Client
#    base64-encodes "Basic <username> <password>" itself, so {{key}}/{{secret}} are never hand-encoded.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth/token
Authorization: Basic {{key}} {{secret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Discovery (FR-FEAT-2, FR-TEST-1).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Discovery: the API root document
GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. A descriptor read (FR-TEST-1). Descriptors are loaded on both templates, so this always returns
#    rows, even on a freshly started minimal environment.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Descriptor list
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/gradeLevelDescriptors?limit=5&totalCount=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Write and read-back (FR-TEST-1). FeederSchoolAssociation needs no descriptor and no student --
#    just two schools that already exist in the baseline hierarchy -- so it is safe on a freshly
#    bootstrapped minimal environment. Its natural key (schoolId + feederSchoolId + beginDate) is
#    fixed, and DMS upserts on a matching natural key, so re-running this file returns 200 (not a
#    duplicate) instead of failing on a second run.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Write: the middle school feeds into the high school
# @name writeFeederSchool
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/feederSchoolAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": {{highSchoolId}} },
  "feederSchoolReference": { "schoolId": {{middleSchoolId}} },
  "beginDate": "2024-08-01"
}

### Read-back, by the same natural key
# @name readFeederSchool
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/feederSchoolAssociations?schoolId={{highSchoolId}}&feederSchoolId={{middleSchoolId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Full paged extract: limit/offset with totalCount (FR-FEAT-7, FR-TEST-6).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Paging: limit/offset, with Total-Count in the response headers
# @name pageOne
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/gradeLevelDescriptors?limit=5&offset=0&totalCount=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Cursor paging (FR-FEAT-8, FR-TEST-6). The first pageToken comes from the Next-Page-Token header
#    on the limit= response above, or from GET .../partitions -- pageSize alone, with no token,
#    returns 400 "PageToken is required when pageSize is specified." (spike-notes.md Q8).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Cursor paging: the next page, using the token from request 5's Next-Page-Token header
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/gradeLevelDescriptors?pageSize=5&pageToken={{pageOne.response.headers.Next-Page-Token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Incremental extract: change queries (FR-FEAT-4, FR-TEST-6). availableChangeVersions gives the
#    window bounds; a minChangeVersion/maxChangeVersion query then extracts only what changed in it.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Change query: the available change-version window
# @name changeVersions
GET {{baseUrl}}/changeQueries/v1/availableChangeVersions
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### Change query: an incremental extract of that window
GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/gradeLevelDescriptors?minChangeVersion={{changeVersions.response.body.oldestChangeVersion}}&maxChangeVersion={{changeVersions.response.body.newestChangeVersion}}&totalCount=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. ETag (FR-FEAT-6). If-Match with the current ETag succeeds (204, with a new ETag). Reusing that
#    now-stale ETag on a second update returns 412 "Optimistic Lock Failed" (spike-notes.md Q8).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### ETag: If-Match with the current ETag from request 4's read-back -- expect 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/feederSchoolAssociations/{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0._etag}}"

{
  "id": "{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0.id}}",
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": {{highSchoolId}} },
  "feederSchoolReference": { "schoolId": {{middleSchoolId}} },
  "beginDate": "2024-08-01",
  "endDate": "2025-06-30"
}

### ETag: reusing the now-stale ETag from request 4 -- expect 412 Optimistic Lock Failed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/feederSchoolAssociations/{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0._etag}}"

{
  "id": "{{readFeederSchool.response.body.0.id}}",
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": {{highSchoolId}} },
  "feederSchoolReference": { "schoolId": {{middleSchoolId}} },
  "beginDate": "2024-08-01",
  "endDate": "2026-06-30"
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. A deliberately invalid request (FR-TEST-3): a school with no id, no category, and no grade
#    levels. Expect 400 with a body listing each missing field.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Deliberately invalid: missing every required field on a school
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameOfInstitution": "Missing required fields on purpose"
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Assessment-style reference write (FR-TEST-7) -- REQUIRES THE POPULATED TEMPLATE.
#
# The bootstrap (ADMIN) credential used everywhere above is scoped only to SEA 99
# (bootstrap/README.md), and EdFiSandbox reads people through RelationshipsWithEdOrgsAndPeople, so it
# cannot list or resolve students outside its own hierarchy -- there is no request this file can run
# with that credential to discover a real studentUniqueId from the populated sample data
# (spike-notes.md Q7). To run this one for real:
#
#   1. Provision an assessment-shaped credential scoped to the sample LEA:
#      `new-credential --shape assessment --edorg-ids 255901` (Task 13).
#   2. Get a token for it (repeat request 1 above with that credential's key/secret instead of
#      {{key}}/{{secret}}).
#   3. GET {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/students?limit=1 with that token to find a real studentUniqueId.
#   4. Paste it in place of REPLACE-WITH-POPULATED-STUDENT-ID below.
#
# Left as-is, or run against the minimal template (which has no students at all), DMS returns
# 400 or 409 naming the unresolved reference -- for example a message citing "StudentReference" or
# "StudentUniqueId" -- rather than an ambiguous empty success (FR-TEST-8).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### requires populated: enroll an existing student (by natural key) in a baseline school
POST {{baseUrl}}/data/ed-fi/studentSchoolAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "REPLACE-WITH-POPULATED-STUDENT-ID" },
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": {{elementarySchoolId}} },
  "entryDate": "2024-08-01",
  "entryGradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Kindergarten"
}
